            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="0709" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.20 Missions/11: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-03T16:00:00+03:06">May 3, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 4—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. Department’s 80, May 1, 5 p.m.<anchor n="97" xml:id="d764-f1"/> Colonel
                    Garret B. Shomber was presented to King April 23 as chief of United States
                    military <pb facs="0710" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/> mission. I fear grave
                    weakening of American standing and influence with King Ibn Saud if United States
                    mission now withdrawn and British-led mission replaces it. If Department intends
                    effectively to defend oil reserves here such considerations cannot be
                    ignored.</p>
                <p>The King in discussing military mission never indicated any preference for Moslem
                    instructors. Please confirm that Department wishes me in concert with British
                    Minister to obtain King’s consent in change in mission.</p>
                <p>Because of overwhelming American economic interests in Saudi Arabia, British
                    should recognize American priority in economic and financial missions’ advisers
                    and experts without necessity of bargaining.</p>
                <p>Code text to Cairo airmail for Giles.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
